WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.840
Closed loop agent tests show that naming the right Xiangqi move succeeds in only 13.9% of trials once an engine defender responds. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 194. Xiangqi bench tests whether language model agents can actually deliver checkmate against an engine defender in 119 tactical end-games. Researchers recorded 8,568 multi-turn trajectories from 12 frontier models. Models played the stored

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:37.520
reference first move in 26.1% of sighted trials, yet only 13.9% of those trials ended in a win.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:44.720
The leading model reached 38.7% pass at 3, but only 5.9% pass cubed,

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.900
winning all three trials on just 7 of the 46 positions it ever solved.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:55.160
32.3% of accepted simulation calls stopped on an illegal move,

00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:02.260
and in 49.3% of comparable cases, the real defender replied differently from the line the agent simulated.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:10.020
Hakim Bench version 1.0 supplies 2,346 items and 4,275 choice.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.300
Yes, no, and score questions across seven tracks.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.440
A single harness scores decision quality via macro F1, calibration via normalized briar score,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:25.740
4, and selective automation by a normalized area under the generalized risk coverage curve,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.360
then combines the 3 by geometric mean with 2,000 bootstrap intervals.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.860
On a board of 16 rows, the leader reaches a composite of 0.888, while the submitting

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:46.240
labs model sits 7th at 0.660 on all tracks, and 6th at 0.678 when restricted to the 4 non-contaminated

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:46.660
tracks.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:55.100
SimCE supplies 4,707 false undergraduate algebra and real analysis conjectures, each paired

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.260
with an executable Python verifier that doubles as the reward function.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:06.000
Training Quinn-34B with supervised fine-tuning on counter-examples alone collapses true

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:14.240
theorem recognition from 0.27 to 0.00, while GRPO with sparse outcome-only reward raises it

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:21.880
to 0.66. The collapse replicates on Gemma 34b, and the resulting 4b model outperforms every

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:27.400
evaluated 7b open weights math specialist, while staying competitive with six frontier

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:33.580
commercial APIs on GSM 8K, math 500, and MMLU college math.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:40.940
Finn Dialog Lens combines compact fine-tuned classifiers that detect RFQ triggers and price

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:45.200
or trade metadata, with an RFQ level module and trade engine.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:53.160
GPT-40 reaches 92.1% accuracy on final price and 94.3% on trade outcome.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:59.220
A difficulty aware router allocates requests between a rule-based engine and the LLM trade

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:06.360
engine, cutting LLM calls by 85% on final price while recovering half the accuracy gap and

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:10.980
saving over $300 per day at 70,000 RFQ daily scale.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.960
Fine-tuned open-source models as small as 3B parameters achieve comparable performance

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.820
with modest, in-domain data.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:26.020
SBIRT 2S1 converts sentence-transformers and coders into buy-in-coder, cross-head and

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.120
prior-fused residual decision models.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:34.520
Retrieval training improves zero-shot matching of content-bearing options and, after fine-tuning,

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:41.160
significantly helps the prior fused residual head in 10 of 15 comparisons across 5 pairs and 3

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:47.040
training set sizes. The crosshead architecture outperforms the prior fused residual head under

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:54.820
every training objective, and a human audit of 177 verifier decisions finds 97.7% accuracy.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:04:01.280
Sigma is the first large scale 3 billion 8 billion continuous diffusion language model built on

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.020
Steerable low-dimensional ODE-SDE latent trajectories.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:10.300
After pre-training, it matches discrete mass diffusion and autoregressive baselines

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:14.780
on GSM 8K, Minerva, Human Eval, and MBPP.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:21.000
After supervised fine-tuning, it remains competitive on Math 500 and AIME.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.380
Classifier-free guidance and score temperature prove essential for high fidelity reasoning

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:31.260
and coding, while embedding space steering governs the quality diversity trade-off.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:37.200
off. Calibrated user embeddings encode observed sessions and sample continuous representations

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.740
that decode into persona commands without any training step.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:47.220
On Towsquared Bench, the simulators commit fewer simulator attributed errors and more faithfully

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:53.240
reproduce real user agent failure modes. Aggregate success rates and outcomes for specific task

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:58.620
user pairs. After fitting mostly to customer support interactions, the same simulators

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:04.760
generalize to document creation, math tutoring, and casual conversation across different simulator

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:12.260
LLMs. APD-MEM represents conversation history as four progressively detailed layers, thematic

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:18.800
summaries, personalized key facts, turn-level evidence notes, and raw messages. A controller

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:24.580
applies progressive disclosure, so simple queries terminate early, while complex temporal or

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.800
to hop queries triggered deeper inspection.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:33.120
On Long Mem evil, the architecture achieves strong performance while accessing only 8% of

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.120
total conversations.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:40.260
EpiWorld grounds an LLM policy actor in a learned action-conditioned epidemiological

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:44.140
world model and a tiered skill library of public health protocols.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:50.180
The world model achieves the best out-of-distribution peak MAE among forecasting baselines.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:56.980
The closed-loop framework reduces cumulative hospitalization by up to 59% across COVID-19

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:03.580
and influenza data sets, and by an average of approximately 16% across six LLM backbones.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.700
Plan pool externalizes the clarification plan as a mutable question pool,

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.440
that every planned question must be explicitly asked or dropped before submission.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:19.980
A cross-3 benchmarks derived from bird interact and spider, the approach improves ambiguity

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:26.020
coverage and reduces silent failures over unconstrained and prompt-based alternatives while maintaining

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.960
competitive execution accuracy.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:34.920
TPBench evaluates three information targets at shared nominal retention budgets, the user's

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:40.660
initial goal, the current value of a revised slot, and both in dialogues containing a late

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.180
annotated slot update.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:49.200
On the joint probe at 0.30 retained fraction, every tested compressed method remains below

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.540
full context with the main Lama reader.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:57.100
Deleting the turn that carries the update sharply lowers current value accuracy, while

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.000
deleting one matched irrelevant turn leaves it unchanged.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:08.760
Convo Drift contains 15,727 shared multi-turn conversational structures, with six prompt response

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:14.600
pairs per conversation annotated for style drift and style direction. Across seven

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:20.200
Lycret criteria annotated by three human annotators, the average Krippendorf's alpha reaches

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:27.880
0.88. Drift events induce lexical changes while preserving semantic similarity. Many facet

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:33.940
rash models decompose scores into latent summary quality, raider severity, dimension severity,

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.920
and rating-scale thresholds.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:42.000
Across 17 open-weight LLM judges on some of our moderate alignment in latent summary

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.260
quality does not imply alignment in residual hardness.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:51.680
Human and LLM judges differ in which summary dimension units remain difficult, with the mismatch

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.380
strongly dimension-dependent.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:59.320
VLMs generate question modifiers that add non-essential, ambiguous, or false information.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:06.140
In the presence of such violations, chat GPT, Claude, Gemini, and Lava, all show diminished

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:06.740
performance.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:12.640
Human cognitive effort measured through time-on-task is lower for resolving VLM-induced

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:17.440
violations, yet VLMs themselves perform less accurately in those cases.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:23.800
Try running the Shang-Chi Bench Interactive REPL against any frontier model you have API

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:29.060
access to, and measure your own conversion gap between first move accuracy and final

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:35.800
win rate. Download the SIM-CE corpus and verifiers from the linked GitHub repository to test

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:43.420
GRPO training on a 4B class model for counter-example generation. Apply the Fin dialog lens difficulty

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:50.140
aware router pattern to any multi-party dialog task where LLM call volume is the dominant cost driver.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:56.760
Fit calibrated user embeddings on your own customer support logs and evaluate whether the resulting

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:02.040
Simulators reproduce your observed agent failure modes on Towsquared Bench-style tasks.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:07.520
Expect further executable agent benchmarks that score close loop outcomes rather than

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.000
static answer correctness.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:14.040
Watch for additional verifier-driven reinforcement learning environments released alongside

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.580
math and code corpora.

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:21.700
Look for hybrid routing systems that combine rule-based engines with LLM components to appear

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.420
in production, financial, and customer support tooling.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:29.580
Pop the hood on a hierarchical progressive disclosure, and the gap between flat retrieval

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:34.900
and adaptive memory access appears most clearly when query complexity varies inside a single

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:35.880
long conversation.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:41.240
A controller that first reads thematic summaries and only drills into turn-level evidence when

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:44.500
needed creates an automatic cost-fidelity trade-off.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.860
Simple queries terminate after the first layer, while temporal or multi-hop queries expand

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:55.540
to raw messages, cutting total tokens examined to roughly 8% on long-mem eval.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:10:00.520
The engineering cost is an extra synthesis step that consolidates retrieved evidence

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:06.380
and flags contradictions before final generation. When the controller misjudges query difficulty,

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:11.940
the system either wastes tokens on unnecessary detail or returns incomplete context.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:16.960
The practical decision rule is to adopt progressive disclosure whenever average

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:22.580
conversation length exceeds a few thousand tokens, and query types mix factual lookup with

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:23.600
multi-hop reasoning.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:29.580
Before we go, more executable agent benchmarks that score closed loop outcomes are expected

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:30.520
in the coming weeks.

